From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:46:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: restore station flags on association

The DISASSOC event clears wcid.sta and sets wcid.sta_disabled, but the
ASSOC event restores neither. A station that moves from ASSOC to AUTH
and back on the same link reaches the rate control setup with sta
cleared. That setup looks the station up through its wcid with no
NULL check, so the kernel oopses.

Restore both flags at the start of the ASSOC event, before the first
firmware command, so that a re-association sees the same state as a
first association. mt7915 also sets both flags on ASSOC.

Fixes: d71108eedab1 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: Do not set wcid.sta to 1 in mt7996_mac_sta_event()")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/main.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1484,6 +1484,8 @@ mt7996_mac_sta_links_event(struct mt7996
 
 		switch (ev) {
 		case MT76_STA_EVENT_ASSOC:
+			msta_link->wcid.sta = 1;
+			msta_link->wcid.sta_disabled = 0;
 			err = mt7996_mcu_add_sta(dev, link_conf, link_sta,
 						 link, msta_link,
 						 CONN_STATE_CONNECT, true);
